         raise Exception
 
+``wait_exponential_jitter`` adds jitter to an exponential backoff. Like the other
+wait strategies, ``min``, ``max`` and ``jitter`` accept a number of seconds or a
+``datetime.timedelta``.
+
+.. testcode::
+
+    import datetime
+
+    @retry(wait=wait_exponential_jitter(initial=1,
+                                        min=datetime.timedelta(seconds=2),
+                                        max=60,
+                                        jitter=datetime.timedelta(seconds=1)))
+    def wait_exponential_jitter_min():
+        print("Wait at least 2 seconds, then an exponentially growing delay plus up to 1 second of jitter, capped at 60 seconds")
+        raise Exception
+
 
 Sometimes it's necessary to build a chain of backoffs.
 
